---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <!-- 1. Password Lock Gate Screen -->
  <div id="password-gate">
    <div class="lock-box">
      <h2 class="blink">This content is protected</h2>
      <p>Please enter the password to view this page.</p>
      <div class="input-group">
        <input
          type="password"
          id="password-input"
          placeholder="Enter password..."
        />
        <button id="unlock-btn">Unlock</button>
      </div>
      <p id="error-message" class="error-msg"></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 2. Secure Content Layer (Hidden by default) -->
  <div id="secure-content" style="display: none;">
    <h1>Philosophies</h1>

    <h2>Amito.Buddhism</h2>
    <p>
      It all started in the north of India, Himachal Pradesh, Dharamshala.
      Sitting just at the beginning of the Himalayan mountains. I was having
      very chill weeks there. Sitting in restaurants and cafes. Reading,
      writing, laughing, crying all by myself sitting on the floor and eating
      with my hands. Dharamshala is a very holy place for the Tibetan Buddhists.
      The Dalai Lama the supreme leader of the Tibetan Buddhists lives there and
      I was very lucky to have a chance to see him. I woke up that day, went to
      the temple saw him with all the ceremonies and later that day started a 10
      day Tibetan Buddhism retreat. No phones/ technology, no talking (almost)
      ~3 of meditation every day, 5 hours of Buddhist teachings every day. In
      those 10 days I felt the clearness of my mind very vibrantly, I was having
      very deep realizations and Insights about myself and the world. Since then
      I've been pretty committed to daily meditations and started using the
      buddhist tools taught from the Dharma very efficiently and they were very
      efficient in finding calmness, focus, happiness, and clarity in my daily
      life.
    </p>

    <h2>Balanced Ambition</h2>
    <p>
      I want to use my skills and strengths to do big stuff. To express myself
      and to help others. It's easy for me to start working about something, and
      quickly feel stressed and stiff. I call it toxic hyperfocus. Seems like
      it's something like adrenaline. I taught myself that this is the way to be
      focused and be productive, assuming it's fine to feel that horrible stress
      in my body. Then I understood that it's a spectrum: Unfocused Flow Toxic
      Hyperfocus I easily get into toxic hyperfocus, I can even feel it right
      now when I'm writing this. The main two things I remind myself are: Be
      Royal - I deserve the best, I want to service myself the best I can.
      stressing myself out is neither pleasurable or useful. See Badolina for
      more Observe - see your body and brain experiencing this. In other words
      your mind observing your experience. In other words meditation. See
      Amito.Buddhism for more
    </p>

    <h2>Meaning</h2>
    <p>
      For me it's all about being happy and doing good. Then, comes the
      challenge of wanting to do good for others but getting burnt out and
      unhappy from that. See Balanced Ambition for more.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>

<!-- Client-side Logic Script Box -->
<script>
  // Set your desired password here
  const CORRECT_PASSWORD = "BuddhismIsTrash";

  // Crucial: 'astro:page-load' ensures this fires perfectly on initial load
  // AND whenever navigating via client-side links without a hard refresh.
  document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", () => {
    const passwordGate = document.getElementById("password-gate");
    const secureContent = document.getElementById("secure-content");
    const passwordInput = document.getElementById(
      "password-input",
    ) as HTMLInputElement;
    const unlockBtn = document.getElementById("unlock-btn");
    const errorMessage = document.getElementById("error-message");

    // Exit cleanly if we are on a page that doesn't render these password elements
    if (!passwordInput || !unlockBtn) return;

    function verifyPassword() {
      if (!passwordInput || !passwordGate || !secureContent || !errorMessage)
        return;

      if (passwordInput.value === CORRECT_PASSWORD) {
        passwordGate.style.display = "none";
        secureContent.style.display = "block";
      } else {
        errorMessage.textContent = "Incorrect password. Try again.";
        passwordInput.value = "";
      }
    }

    // Bind event hooks safely
    unlockBtn.addEventListener("click", verifyPassword);

    passwordInput.addEventListener("keypress", (e) => {
      if (e.key === "Enter") {
        verifyPassword();
      }
    });
  });
</script>
<style>
  /* Centers the password card exactly in the middle of the viewport */
  #password-gate {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 60vh;
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .lock-box {
    background-color: rgb(60, 60, 60);
    padding: 2.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 400px;
    width: 100%;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
  }

  .lock-box h2 {
    color: greenyellow;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .lock-box p {
    color: #ccc;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .input-group {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .input-group input {
    flex-grow: 1;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border: 2px solid #444;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background-color: #222;
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 1rem;
    outline: none;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }

  .input-group input:focus {
    border-color: greenyellow;
  }

  .input-group button {
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    background-color: greenyellow;
    border: none;
    /* border-radius: 10000px; */
    color: #222;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 1rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }

  .input-group button:hover {
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .error-msg {
    color: #ff5252 !important;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0 !important;
    font-weight: 500;
    height: 1.2rem;
  }
</style>
